1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,146
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:05,332
We will bust Penguin
one day, I promise you.

3
00:00:05,439 --> 00:00:06,930
Harvey, we
cannot let this slide.

4
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:09,340
You find someone with
the license, they walk.

5
00:00:09,443 --> 00:00:10,934
Miss Falcone, I need to know

6
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:12,980
that you are not on
some fool's errand

7
00:00:13,046 --> 00:00:14,674
<i>to rebuild your father's empire.</i>

8
00:00:14,748 --> 00:00:16,239
<i>An example needs to be made.</i>

9
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:17,978
SOFIA: <i>You may think
you have everything,</i>

10
00:00:18,051 --> 00:00:19,883
but there is one
thing you don't have.

11
00:00:19,987 --> 00:00:21,216
The Falcone name.

12
00:00:21,321 --> 00:00:23,552
Is that your plan to
get close to Penguin?

13
00:00:23,657 --> 00:00:25,148
Gain his confidence? What then?

14
00:00:25,225 --> 00:00:28,855
I used to be smart,
brilliant, and now it's gone.

15
00:00:31,064 --> 00:00:32,624
MAN: <i>Never seen
nothing like him before.</i>

16
00:00:32,966 --> 00:00:34,127
(GROWLS)

17
00:00:34,535 --> 00:00:35,798
(CHOKING) Who are you?

18
00:00:36,069 --> 00:00:38,163
GRUNDY: <i>Solomon Grundy.</i>

19
00:00:38,405 --> 00:00:41,204
You know Grundy?

20
00:00:41,308 --> 00:00:43,539
We're the very best of friends.

21
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,872
<i>With your muscles,
we can make money.</i>

22
00:00:45,946 --> 00:00:47,539
We'd like to put
our hat in the ring.

23
00:00:47,614 --> 00:00:48,673
Go get the doc.

24
00:00:52,019 --> 00:00:53,850
(CROWD YELLING)

25
00:00:59,393 --> 00:01:00,691
(FIGHTER GRUNTING)

26
00:01:02,162 --> 00:01:03,494
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

27
00:01:06,266 --> 00:01:07,825
(PEOPLE CHEERING)

28
00:01:16,643 --> 00:01:17,770
- (BONE CRACKS)
- (GROANS)

29
00:01:17,878 --> 00:01:18,878
Good as new.

30
00:01:26,887 --> 00:01:31,882
Dr. Lee Thompkins. Oh,
my God. (LAUGHING)

31
00:01:32,259 --> 00:01:34,558
Now, what is a girl like you
doing in a place like this?

32
00:01:34,628 --> 00:01:36,221
I heard a rumor you were frozen.

33
00:01:36,463 --> 00:01:38,398
I should have known it
was too good to be true.

34
00:01:38,765 --> 00:01:40,700
Hey, you're not still
mad at me, are you?

35
00:01:41,268 --> 00:01:42,736
Mad at you for what?

36
00:01:43,203 --> 00:01:45,968
Killing Kristin Kringle,
or framing Jim for murder

37
00:01:46,073 --> 00:01:49,441
so he would be in prison when
I lost our child? (CHUCKLES)

38
00:01:50,744 --> 00:01:53,737
I'm over all that.
Let's be friends.

39
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:58,415
- I'm sensing sarcasm.
- Just as sharp as ever.

40
00:01:59,353 --> 00:02:01,015
Actually it's funny
that you mention that.

41
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:02,248
Good bye, Ed.

42
00:02:02,322 --> 00:02:03,322
Wait.

43
00:02:05,225 --> 00:02:06,225
Holy hell.

44
00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:08,387
Butch Gilzean?

45
00:02:09,563 --> 00:02:10,656
What have you done to him?

46
00:02:10,764 --> 00:02:12,096
Nothing, believe it or not.

47
00:02:12,399 --> 00:02:13,958
And he goes by Grundy now.

48
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:16,059
Hey, why don't you
hang over there, big fella?

49
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:17,798
Making sure that wall
doesn't wander off.

50
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:19,138
(GRUNTS)

51
00:02:23,543 --> 00:02:24,983
I have no idea what
happened to him.

52
00:02:25,045 --> 00:02:27,276
But he's freakishly strong.

53
00:02:27,347 --> 00:02:29,441
Can't remember
anything about his past life

54
00:02:29,616 --> 00:02:32,176
and he seems to love
me, so big improvement.

55
00:02:32,352 --> 00:02:37,689
But I, on the other hand I'm really
hoping to get back to who I was.

56
00:02:38,492 --> 00:02:41,360
When I was on ice my
head got a little scrambled.

57
00:02:41,595 --> 00:02:42,858
Why should I care?

58
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:44,689
Okay, I came here with Grundy.

59
00:02:44,965 --> 00:02:47,628
Gonna fight, make some
money to get me smart again.

60
00:02:47,701 --> 00:02:53,333
But you, Dr. Leslie Thompkins,

61
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:55,472
you can fix me.

62
00:02:56,209 --> 00:02:58,303
You want me to fix you?

63
00:02:59,546 --> 00:03:01,344
Oh, you really are dumb.

64
00:03:01,415 --> 00:03:04,817
Okay, you are here
for some reason.

65
00:03:05,152 --> 00:03:06,882
I don't pretend to
know what that is.

66
00:03:06,987 --> 00:03:12,119
But if you help
me, I will help you.

67
00:03:12,359 --> 00:03:15,955
I know you're not really smart
right now, so try to understand this.

68
00:03:16,697 --> 00:03:18,131
I will never help you.

69
00:03:24,337 --> 00:03:25,937
PENGUIN: I was
raised to be a gentleman.

70
00:03:26,106 --> 00:03:27,426
SOFIA: But you're
also practical.

71
00:03:27,741 --> 00:03:28,741
We were seen at dinner

72
00:03:28,842 --> 00:03:31,175
as we have been
the past three nights.

73
00:03:31,344 --> 00:03:34,109
All of Gotham knows you have
the support of the Falcone family.

74
00:03:34,948 --> 00:03:37,679
And I'm fairly certain no
one's watching us now.

75
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:41,911
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

76
00:03:42,022 --> 00:03:45,720
I just like to know
where I stand.

77
00:03:50,497 --> 00:03:52,056
This isn't easy for me.

78
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:58,971
To have someone I
can trust, a real friend.

79
00:04:02,976 --> 00:04:04,444
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

80
00:04:09,282 --> 00:04:10,511
You can trust me.

81
00:04:13,053 --> 00:04:14,851
Let's have lunch
tomorrow. Just us.

82
00:04:17,858 --> 00:04:18,858
Till then.

83
00:04:34,741 --> 00:04:35,834
Have a nice dinner?

84
00:04:37,978 --> 00:04:39,310
How long have you been here?

85
00:04:39,579 --> 00:04:40,579
Long enough.

86
00:04:40,814 --> 00:04:42,578
It's time you tell me
what you're planning.

87
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:44,479
This again?

88
00:04:45,485 --> 00:04:46,976
Ever since you've
come to Gotham,

89
00:04:47,154 --> 00:04:49,487
all you've done is
make Oswald stronger.

90
00:04:49,589 --> 00:04:50,818
It's time I know your endgame.

91
00:04:52,993 --> 00:04:54,222
And if I refuse?

92
00:04:55,829 --> 00:04:57,422
I'll put you on a train home.

93
00:05:06,006 --> 00:05:07,474
I wanna make you a promise.

94
00:05:08,208 --> 00:05:11,406
In a matter of days, I'll have
Cobblepot in the palm of my hand.

95
00:05:13,079 --> 00:05:17,278
If I fail, I'll stay, I'll
go, whatever you want.

96
00:05:28,395 --> 00:05:29,829
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

97
00:05:31,531 --> 00:05:32,897
Look, the count's good.

98
00:05:33,834 --> 00:05:35,200
Well, now, go
on, get out of here.

99
00:05:35,302 --> 00:05:36,302
See you next month.

100
00:05:44,444 --> 00:05:46,003
(LOUD CRASHING)

101
00:05:47,514 --> 00:05:48,538
Someone down there?

102
00:06:22,148 --> 00:06:23,377
(DOOR CREAKS)

103
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:26,481
(CAT MEOWS)

104
00:06:27,888 --> 00:06:29,288
Freaking cats.

105
00:06:33,026 --> 00:06:34,255
Oink, oink.

106
00:06:35,128 --> 00:06:36,128
What the...

107
00:06:43,036 --> 00:06:45,096
(INDISTINCT CHATTER
ON POLICE RADIO)

108
00:06:45,772 --> 00:06:48,173
- (SIREN WAILING)
- Hi. Is he really one of ours?

109
00:06:48,575 --> 00:06:52,012
Seems so. He was in the uniform,
but the killer took his badge.

110
00:06:52,545 --> 00:06:53,945
No one recognizes him?

111
00:06:54,447 --> 00:06:56,916
Well, that part we
have not figured out, yet.

112
00:06:58,118 --> 00:06:59,211
Let me show ya.

113
00:07:02,756 --> 00:07:03,756
Good God.

114
00:07:03,823 --> 00:07:04,823
Freaky, huh?

115
00:07:05,625 --> 00:07:07,218
Let's find out who this guy is.

116
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,223
Here we go.

117
00:07:16,636 --> 00:07:18,867
Dave Metzger. You know him?

118
00:07:19,306 --> 00:07:20,535
Seen him around.

119
00:07:20,707 --> 00:07:23,404
Not to speak ill of the dead,
but he was a grade A bastard.

120
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:25,210
Did he have
enemies on the force?

121
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:28,305
No, no cop would do this to
another cop and he was a candyman.

122
00:07:29,282 --> 00:07:30,477
Penguin's bagman.

123
00:07:30,583 --> 00:07:33,143
He was the one delivering
payoffs to cops in the precinct.

124
00:07:33,253 --> 00:07:34,516
I mean, that's the rumor.

125
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:37,785
Yeah, so someone killed
him to send a message.

126
00:07:39,292 --> 00:07:40,292
Where are you going?

127
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,360
To see Penguin.

128
00:07:41,461 --> 00:07:43,862
Maybe he knows why someone
wants to kill his employee.

129
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,996
Don't go stirring the pot!

130
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:50,236
WAITRESS: Enjoy your
lunch, Mr. Cobblepot.

131
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:53,329
I need to talk to you.

132
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:56,072
If it takes less than
three minutes I'm all ears.

133
00:07:56,343 --> 00:07:57,777
A cop was murdered last night.

134
00:07:58,778 --> 00:08:02,806
Dave Metzger, a
bagman on your payroll?

135
00:08:02,882 --> 00:08:04,817
Oh, you think I might
know something.

136
00:08:05,452 --> 00:08:08,149
Sadly this is the first
I'm hearing his name.

137
00:08:08,221 --> 00:08:11,020
A general does not need
to know every foot soldier.

138
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:12,622
You don't need to know him.

139
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:15,295
I think someone is trying
to send you a message.

140
00:08:16,763 --> 00:08:18,026
What sort of message.

141
00:08:19,132 --> 00:08:22,694
The killer placed a severed
pig's head over Metzger's own.

142
00:08:23,203 --> 00:08:24,671
Not a very clear message.

143
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:27,967
It could have all
sorts of meanings.

144
00:08:28,208 --> 00:08:30,302
Metzger may have been
dirty, but he was still a cop.

145
00:08:30,443 --> 00:08:31,443
Someone killed him

146
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:33,173
and is using his
death to make a point.

147
00:08:33,413 --> 00:08:35,644
If that is in relation
to you, I need to know.

148
00:08:35,715 --> 00:08:37,411
(CHUCKLES) Jim,

149
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:40,214
if someone had a problem
with me, I would know about it.

150
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,583
And I would deal with it.

151
00:08:44,257 --> 00:08:46,385
Because you're always
one step ahead, Oswald.

152
00:08:47,327 --> 00:08:48,693
It's why I'm alive.

153
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:51,892
But I would like to help.

154
00:08:52,499 --> 00:08:54,491
- Mr. Penn.
- Right here, Mr. Cobblepot.

155
00:08:54,567 --> 00:08:58,595
Do we have anything that could
assist Detective Gordon in doing his job?

156
00:08:58,838 --> 00:09:00,272
As a matter of fact, sir,

157
00:09:00,607 --> 00:09:04,738
a few days ago Mr. Wally Clarke,
applied for a burglary permit...

158
00:09:06,146 --> 00:09:07,580
The Pork Barrel.

159
00:09:07,981 --> 00:09:09,882
It's a butcher on 3rd Street.

160
00:09:09,983 --> 00:09:13,511
- They specialize in offering the...
- Thanks for the lead.

161
00:09:13,586 --> 00:09:15,077
Enjoy your lunch, Oswald.

162
00:09:15,722 --> 00:09:17,156
PENGUIN: Don't thank me, Jim.

163
00:09:17,357 --> 00:09:19,656
Thank the licensing
system you hate so much.

164
00:09:21,327 --> 00:09:24,855
Now, be sure to let me know
if I need to get more involved.

165
00:09:26,166 --> 00:09:28,658
Till then, I'm
rooting for you, Jim.

166
00:09:31,771 --> 00:09:34,172
(OPERATIC MUSIC
PLAYING ON RADIO)

167
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,874
Have a seat, Wally.

168
00:10:10,043 --> 00:10:12,069
You know how much
trouble you're in? Huh?

169
00:10:12,812 --> 00:10:14,713
You know what
we do to cop killers?

170
00:10:14,781 --> 00:10:16,306
I just told him, I
didn't kill nobody.

171
00:10:16,416 --> 00:10:17,884
Specifically not no cop.

172
00:10:17,951 --> 00:10:20,443
Oh, so you didn't lure
Dave Metzger into that alley,

173
00:10:20,553 --> 00:10:22,954
split open his skull and
stick a pig's head on him?

174
00:10:23,056 --> 00:10:25,321
What? (CHUCKLES) Are you crazy?

175
00:10:25,725 --> 00:10:28,786
That's funny. Because we searched
the dumpster behind your apartment

176
00:10:29,429 --> 00:10:30,920
and guess what we found.

177
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:32,890
HARVEY: Whoa-ho!

178
00:10:32,966 --> 00:10:35,231
Look at that. Porky
don't have no head.

179
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:37,365
What do you wanna bet?

180
00:10:38,171 --> 00:10:41,801
That head was on
the dead cop we found.

181
00:10:42,275 --> 00:10:44,437
Screw it. I have enough.

182
00:10:44,611 --> 00:10:45,840
I don't need a confession.

183
00:10:45,945 --> 00:10:48,107
I'm charging you with the
murder of Dave Metzger.

184
00:10:48,181 --> 00:10:50,616
Wait, no! It wasn't me.

185
00:10:52,619 --> 00:10:55,054
- It must have been the Prof.
- Who?

186
00:10:55,455 --> 00:10:58,789
The Professor. That's what I called
him, because he talked all fancy.

187
00:10:58,858 --> 00:11:00,724
He was the one who got
me to rob the butchers.

188
00:11:00,827 --> 00:11:02,728
We need a name, a description.

189
00:11:02,829 --> 00:11:04,695
We did it all over the
phone. The whole deal.

190
00:11:04,864 --> 00:11:06,856
I dropped the heads
under the midtown bridge,

191
00:11:06,966 --> 00:11:08,662
the money was there.
I never met the guy.

192
00:11:08,768 --> 00:11:09,768
Never got no name.

193
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:11,702
What do you mean
"heads"? As in more than one?

194
00:11:11,804 --> 00:11:13,272
How many did this guy want?

195
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:14,339
There's four.

196
00:11:15,041 --> 00:11:16,339
To think he could have told me

197
00:11:16,442 --> 00:11:18,001
that he only needed
the heads, but no.

198
00:11:18,111 --> 00:11:20,478
I had to drag them to my
house, chop the heads off...

199
00:11:20,547 --> 00:11:21,674
Just shut up.

200
00:11:25,185 --> 00:11:26,346
Do you know what this means?

201
00:11:26,452 --> 00:11:28,387
Yeah. Means there's
three more victims out there.

202
00:11:28,988 --> 00:11:31,321
How many bagmen did
Penguin have in the GCPD?

203
00:11:31,391 --> 00:11:34,122
Wild guess, I'd say four. The
only one I knew was Metzger.

204
00:11:35,128 --> 00:11:37,859
Yeah, well the people who
got paid by those bagmen,

205
00:11:38,064 --> 00:11:39,293
they'll know who they are.

206
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,526
They're not gonna talk.

207
00:11:41,067 --> 00:11:42,194
We'll make them.

208
00:11:43,102 --> 00:11:45,071
Hey, don't leave me
back here with this thing.

209
00:11:45,705 --> 00:11:46,705
Hey!

210
00:11:50,743 --> 00:11:52,041
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)

211
00:11:58,117 --> 00:11:59,117
She's not coming.

212
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:02,445
- What?
- Sofia.

213
00:12:02,555 --> 00:12:03,682
Your lunch date.

214
00:12:04,224 --> 00:12:05,224
It's not a date.

215
00:12:05,291 --> 00:12:08,523
Whatever. She called,
she's not coming.

216
00:12:09,896 --> 00:12:11,091
Did she say why?

217
00:12:11,531 --> 00:12:14,558
Something came up, I
don't know. I wasn't listening.

218
00:12:19,772 --> 00:12:20,933
It's just gonna go to waste.

219
00:12:23,076 --> 00:12:25,170
I want you to follow her
and find out who she's with.

220
00:12:25,612 --> 00:12:27,103
You think she's two timing you?

221
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,680
She and I are not...

222
00:12:31,117 --> 00:12:34,554
This lunch was her idea. Now,
she cancels all of a sudden.

223
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:38,186
I want to know why. That's all.

224
00:12:43,396 --> 00:12:44,659
Now, Victor!

225
00:12:44,897 --> 00:12:45,921
(APPLAUSE AND CHEERING)

226
00:12:45,999 --> 00:12:49,299
Today, we have
ourselves a treat.

227
00:12:49,736 --> 00:12:54,401
Our beloved, Hammer, will
take on a new challenger.

228
00:12:55,341 --> 00:12:56,775
Just in from...

229
00:12:58,144 --> 00:13:00,477
- Grundy come from swamp.
- (CROWD LAUGHS)

230
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:03,948
Rules are simple.
Last man standing wins.

231
00:13:04,017 --> 00:13:07,146
Besides that, anything goes.

232
00:13:07,654 --> 00:13:09,179
(CROWD CHEERING)

233
00:13:11,524 --> 00:13:13,254
Whoo-hoo!

234
00:13:17,830 --> 00:13:18,830
Fight!

235
00:13:26,139 --> 00:13:27,139
(GRUNTS)

236
00:13:38,818 --> 00:13:40,252
(YELLING)

237
00:13:41,688 --> 00:13:42,849
(ALL CHEERING)

238
00:13:45,558 --> 00:13:47,527
What are you doing? Fight!

239
00:13:48,795 --> 00:13:49,854
Grundy fight now?

240
00:13:49,962 --> 00:13:51,453
Yes, now.

241
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:18,984
CROWD: (CHANTING) Grundy,
Grundy, Grundy, Grundy, Grundy, Grundy...

242
00:14:20,293 --> 00:14:22,524
Yes, yes!

243
00:14:23,162 --> 00:14:25,188
Yes! Grundy, Ed's best friend.

244
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:32,296
Looks like I got a new cash cow.

245
00:14:33,973 --> 00:14:35,407
Take good care of him, Doc.

246
00:14:36,576 --> 00:14:37,976
And clean up what's
left of Hammer.

247
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:44,293
HARVEY: We're not
looking to bust nobody.

248
00:14:44,317 --> 00:14:47,879
We just want the name of the
bagman who delivers Penguin's money.

249
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:50,546
Don't know what you're talking
about, man. I wish I could help.

250
00:14:50,623 --> 00:14:54,185
- Oh, yeah!
- Hey, hey... Whoa, whoa. Relax.

251
00:14:54,694 --> 00:14:56,458
I know a couple of
other guys we can talk to

252
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:57,962
who aren't such
a douche nozzles.

253
00:14:59,532 --> 00:15:02,058
Seems like you should be looking
for whoever killed Dave Metzger

254
00:15:02,135 --> 00:15:03,569
instead of shaking
down other cops.

255
00:15:03,636 --> 00:15:06,128
I'm trying to save other cops.
More lives are on the line here.

256
00:15:06,239 --> 00:15:07,639
And all you're using is a cop

257
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:10,073
getting killed to go
on a fishing expedition.

258
00:15:10,143 --> 00:15:12,442
(SNIFFS) Smells like IA to me.

259
00:15:13,813 --> 00:15:16,647
Come on. Just say you're
not helping. We get it, okay?

260
00:15:16,916 --> 00:15:17,916
Get off me.

261
00:15:18,351 --> 00:15:20,718
HARVEY: We're trying to
stop cops from getting killed.

262
00:15:20,887 --> 00:15:22,753
How can none of
you nitwits see that?

263
00:15:23,256 --> 00:15:26,055
You're asking a cop to
snitch on another cop.

264
00:15:26,125 --> 00:15:27,753
It ain't gonna happen. (SCOFFS)

265
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:31,353
- Fine. We'll do it your way.
- Yeah.

266
00:15:31,731 --> 00:15:32,960
(GRUNTS)

267
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,600
Oh, jeez!

268
00:15:36,903 --> 00:15:38,201
Whoo!

269
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:43,709
- It's gonna be a hot one today, huh?
- Oh. Yeah. It's gotta be 90 out here.

270
00:15:44,310 --> 00:15:46,404
A lot hotter in there.
Probably a 100.

271
00:15:46,479 --> 00:15:47,970
CULPEPPER: Let
me out, you bastards.

272
00:15:48,981 --> 00:15:51,815
You know what, Jim. I
think we forgot to get lunch.

273
00:15:52,351 --> 00:15:53,512
Think we got time?

274
00:15:55,354 --> 00:15:56,617
I could go out for a burger.

275
00:15:56,689 --> 00:15:57,782
All right, Culpepper.

276
00:15:57,857 --> 00:15:59,758
We're gonna be back
in a couple of hours.

277
00:16:00,326 --> 00:16:01,817
CULPEPPER: Hold it. Let me out!

278
00:16:02,161 --> 00:16:07,793
I'm warning you.
Bullock! Bullock? Bullock!

279
00:16:08,301 --> 00:16:09,530
Okay!

280
00:16:09,669 --> 00:16:10,864
(BANGING ON TRUNK)

281
00:16:13,105 --> 00:16:14,300
(PANTING)

282
00:16:14,373 --> 00:16:15,466
Chris Whitlock.

283
00:16:15,541 --> 00:16:18,705
Makes deliveries for the west
side, but don't say I told you.

284
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:20,040
Where can we find him?

285
00:16:20,146 --> 00:16:21,808
He's supposed to
be in court all day.

286
00:16:23,249 --> 00:16:26,310
My contact on the south side
said the bagman is Jennie Butler.

287
00:16:26,419 --> 00:16:27,580
- Trying to reach her.
- Good.

288
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:30,790
I just wanna find this guy Whitlock.
Hope he gives us the last name.

289
00:16:30,857 --> 00:16:32,348
Should be getting
out of court soon.

290
00:16:32,458 --> 00:16:33,949
You ever think you'd
be running around

291
00:16:34,026 --> 00:16:35,961
trying to save cops
on Penguin's payroll?

292
00:16:36,329 --> 00:16:37,329
Bad cops.

293
00:16:37,530 --> 00:16:40,261
They deserve to be prosecuted
and stripped of their badges.

294
00:16:40,333 --> 00:16:41,333
Not butchered.

295
00:16:41,434 --> 00:16:42,993
(WOMAN SCREAMING)

296
00:16:46,272 --> 00:16:47,433
WOMAN: Call the police!

297
00:17:00,219 --> 00:17:01,585
(POLICE RADIO CHATTER)

298
00:17:05,091 --> 00:17:07,151
A hundred thousand
people in a square mile

299
00:17:07,226 --> 00:17:08,558
and of course
nobody saw nothing.

300
00:17:08,661 --> 00:17:09,720
Or is willing to admit it.

301
00:17:11,697 --> 00:17:15,065
Butler got off duty last night and
not seen since she clocked out.

302
00:17:15,601 --> 00:17:19,060
Whitlock was due in court
at 9:00, but he never showed.

303
00:17:20,273 --> 00:17:23,471
So, they were both abducted,
taken somewhere, killed,

304
00:17:23,543 --> 00:17:25,478
then brought to pose
in front of this building.

305
00:17:25,545 --> 00:17:26,740
Probably for us to find.

306
00:17:26,846 --> 00:17:28,314
It's a hell of a lot of work.

307
00:17:28,581 --> 00:17:30,379
The killer believes his
message is important.

308
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:32,852
What? That he's gotta
rid the city of dirty cops?

309
00:17:32,919 --> 00:17:34,649
Specifically the ones
who work for Penguin.

310
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,086
No wonder these
guys look on edge.

311
00:17:37,757 --> 00:17:40,249
Where are we on our fourth
bagman? We need an ID.

312
00:17:40,359 --> 00:17:41,691
I'm working on it.

313
00:17:48,834 --> 00:17:50,029
(SAXOPHONE PLAYING)

314
00:17:59,779 --> 00:18:01,077
GORDON: Good afternoon, sir.

315
00:18:01,814 --> 00:18:02,873
Sir.

316
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:06,647
Detective James Gordon, GCPD.

317
00:18:07,486 --> 00:18:08,977
You've been playing
here all morning?

318
00:18:10,590 --> 00:18:11,922
On and off, you know.

319
00:18:12,458 --> 00:18:14,290
A guy's gotta take a
break every now and then.

320
00:18:14,393 --> 00:18:16,794
Yeah, sure. Did
you see anything?

321
00:18:17,496 --> 00:18:18,657
Anything out of the usual?

322
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:21,067
Sorry, uh, Detective.

323
00:18:21,667 --> 00:18:23,226
I ain't seen nothing
since the war.

324
00:18:23,669 --> 00:18:27,106
- Right. All right. Have a good one.
- Yeah.

325
00:18:32,311 --> 00:18:35,042
(CLICKS TONGUE) Oh, man. Really?

326
00:18:35,815 --> 00:18:36,942
Let's try this again.

327
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:40,245
Did you see anything?

328
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:44,587
An old van. Filippelli
Plumbing on the side.

329
00:18:45,758 --> 00:18:47,886
Parked up the street a
good part of the morning.

330
00:18:49,061 --> 00:18:51,621
- Guy just sitting in there.
- Guy, what did he look like?

331
00:18:51,964 --> 00:18:54,456
White dude. Didn't see his face.

332
00:18:54,767 --> 00:18:57,669
I took a break, I came
back, the van was gone.

333
00:18:59,205 --> 00:19:00,366
All right. Thanks.

334
00:19:00,473 --> 00:19:01,532
Keep the tip.

335
00:19:05,044 --> 00:19:06,672
(STAPLER CLICKING)

336
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:12,614
What happened to
you, Butch? Grundy?

337
00:19:15,488 --> 00:19:16,649
Look at your hand.

338
00:19:16,722 --> 00:19:19,055
They grew back. How
is that even possible?

339
00:19:20,159 --> 00:19:23,061
Look at this. It's
not even blood.

340
00:19:25,297 --> 00:19:26,822
It's like swamp water.

341
00:19:28,601 --> 00:19:30,968
Grundy from swamp.

342
00:19:31,303 --> 00:19:34,432
Yeah, I heard. You know, you
don't even have a heartbeat.

343
00:19:36,375 --> 00:19:37,707
But you seem to be doing okay.

344
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:43,946
You know, Ed is not your friend.

345
00:19:44,316 --> 00:19:45,614
He's just using you.

346
00:19:46,218 --> 00:19:49,552
No. Ed, Grundy friend.

347
00:19:50,289 --> 00:19:52,849
Ed, Grundy best friend.

348
00:19:52,958 --> 00:19:54,038
He just wants you to fight,

349
00:19:54,126 --> 00:19:57,119
so he can make money and
make his brain better again.

350
00:19:57,830 --> 00:20:00,270
Once he doesn't need you
anymore, he's just gonna discard you.

351
00:20:00,399 --> 00:20:03,062
Or kill you, if that's
even possible.

352
00:20:04,370 --> 00:20:05,770
Do you understand?

353
00:20:07,073 --> 00:20:08,939
Ed, Grundy best friend.

354
00:20:09,241 --> 00:20:10,241
NYGMA: That's right.

355
00:20:11,577 --> 00:20:13,739
Best buddies. A team.

356
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:20,577
Not to mention, your
boss's biggest new attraction.

357
00:20:24,123 --> 00:20:26,058
Smells like we're
sticking around for a while.

358
00:20:26,692 --> 00:20:27,692
Fabulous.

359
00:20:29,929 --> 00:20:31,090
Unless of course,

360
00:20:31,197 --> 00:20:33,757
you're gonna fix the broken
connection in this noodle.

361
00:20:34,033 --> 00:20:36,332
Then we wouldn't have
to stick around. We'd be...

362
00:20:39,839 --> 00:20:40,863
- Gone.
- Yes, thank you.

363
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:42,772
- That's the word you're looking for?
- Yeah.

364
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:45,442
Of course, I'd pay you.

365
00:20:49,949 --> 00:20:53,613
(SIGHS) I'm patching up Grundy
as long as Cherry tells me to.

366
00:20:53,719 --> 00:20:55,915
That's it. Keep your money.

367
00:20:56,856 --> 00:20:58,381
CHERRY: How's
my best new fighter?

368
00:21:00,292 --> 00:21:02,261
He's gonna be ready
to go again tonight, Doc?

369
00:21:02,762 --> 00:21:03,786
Yeah, sure.

370
00:21:04,163 --> 00:21:05,995
I gotta step out for
a while. I'll be back.

371
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:09,433
Just make sure you're here.
We got a deal you know?

372
00:21:09,502 --> 00:21:10,663
Yeah. I know.

373
00:21:13,239 --> 00:21:14,298
(DOOR OPENS)

374
00:21:17,576 --> 00:21:18,771
(PATIENTS COUGHING)

375
00:21:23,182 --> 00:21:24,182
Hi, everyone.

376
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:27,677
I'm sorry to have kept you
waiting. I'll be right with you. Okay?

377
00:21:41,066 --> 00:21:42,659
Right. You can come on in.

378
00:21:49,074 --> 00:21:50,269
Sit right there.

379
00:21:51,811 --> 00:21:53,473
I'll help you up.
One, two, three!

380
00:22:02,822 --> 00:22:04,450
Let's have a listen.

381
00:22:13,232 --> 00:22:14,996
(CHUCKLES)

382
00:22:15,668 --> 00:22:17,000
(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)

383
00:22:37,122 --> 00:22:40,991
Sofia Falcone,
what are you doing?

384
00:22:45,331 --> 00:22:46,458
HARVEY: Yeah. All right.

385
00:22:47,233 --> 00:22:48,633
That was the Mayor's office.

386
00:22:48,734 --> 00:22:51,203
Press has gotten wind.
Things are gonna heat up fast.

387
00:22:51,470 --> 00:22:52,699
Then we catch him fast.

388
00:22:53,038 --> 00:22:54,666
All the cops who
haven't called in.

389
00:22:56,876 --> 00:23:01,371
Han, Petersen, King,
Nakajima, Massengill.

390
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:03,506
Yeah, so the precinct's
already looking for them,

391
00:23:03,582 --> 00:23:06,416
but I say we take this list to
Penguin, have him point to a name.

392
00:23:06,518 --> 00:23:09,078
No need. Nakajima is the bagman.

393
00:23:09,889 --> 00:23:10,948
How do you know?

394
00:23:11,056 --> 00:23:13,582
Petersen and Massengill are
both hardcore Bible thumpers.

395
00:23:13,692 --> 00:23:17,288
That leaves three. And
I've heard Nakajima is dirty.

396
00:23:17,396 --> 00:23:20,298
Units are already on the way to
his apartment, same as the others.

397
00:23:20,399 --> 00:23:22,698
I say we retrace his beat,
concentrate our resources.

398
00:23:22,768 --> 00:23:23,792
Hold on.

399
00:23:28,207 --> 00:23:30,301
Doesn't something about
this feel weird to you?

400
00:23:30,476 --> 00:23:33,105
Whoever set the trap for
Metzger, knew where he'd be.

401
00:23:33,312 --> 00:23:36,248
And the killer also knew
Butler and Whitlock's schedules.

402
00:23:36,682 --> 00:23:38,082
Are you saying
it's one of our own?

403
00:23:38,183 --> 00:23:39,776
Someone who's fed
up with the corruption

404
00:23:39,885 --> 00:23:40,909
decided to make a stand.

405
00:23:41,220 --> 00:23:43,587
But to kill them and display
their bodies that way?

406
00:23:43,689 --> 00:23:47,182
I know, brother, but it's something
we at least have to consider.

407
00:23:47,459 --> 00:23:49,219
Which means anything
that we say out there...

408
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:50,285
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

409
00:23:50,763 --> 00:23:53,528
We got a lead on the plumbing
van your blind man saw.

410
00:23:53,599 --> 00:23:55,693
It was spotted near the
abandoned dairy on Commerce.

411
00:23:55,768 --> 00:23:57,031
Should we get the strike force?

412
00:23:57,102 --> 00:23:58,365
No. Gordon and I will cover it.

413
00:23:58,437 --> 00:24:00,269
If we need backup,
I'll give you a call.

414
00:24:00,539 --> 00:24:02,440
And until then,
don't say a word.

415
00:24:02,541 --> 00:24:03,873
And that's an order. You got it?

416
00:24:04,877 --> 00:24:06,209
Let's go. Come on.

417
00:24:33,105 --> 00:24:35,097
(BREATHING HEAVILY
AND WHIMPERING)

418
00:24:35,174 --> 00:24:36,699
Oink, oink.

419
00:24:37,476 --> 00:24:39,138
Little piggy.

420
00:24:42,848 --> 00:24:44,407
(GROWLS)

421
00:25:01,266 --> 00:25:02,529
(CHEERING)

422
00:25:17,383 --> 00:25:18,976
(GRUNTING)

423
00:25:34,199 --> 00:25:40,105
Our new champion.

424
00:25:40,406 --> 00:25:41,897
(ALL CHEERING)

425
00:25:47,513 --> 00:25:48,879
(CROWD CHANTING)

426
00:25:54,319 --> 00:25:56,652
ZSASZ: So it turns out Sofia
broke her date with you...

427
00:25:56,722 --> 00:25:58,315
It was not a date!

428
00:25:59,258 --> 00:26:00,556
To have lunch with the mayor.

429
00:26:02,094 --> 00:26:03,255
They went to Angelo's.

430
00:26:03,595 --> 00:26:05,996
She had the lobster
ravioli, he had the tagliatelle.

431
00:26:06,198 --> 00:26:10,533
After they parted ways, Sofia went
to the old Gotham Heritage Hotel.

432
00:26:10,936 --> 00:26:13,235
I don't understand. That
place has been vacant for years.

433
00:26:13,305 --> 00:26:16,070
If I may. A couple of
months ago I'd gotten word

434
00:26:16,141 --> 00:26:20,408
a secret buyer had purchased
the hotel at six percent over asking.

435
00:26:20,746 --> 00:26:23,238
I think it's safe to assume
that buyer was Miss Falcone.

436
00:26:23,949 --> 00:26:25,281
But why?

437
00:26:25,384 --> 00:26:28,912
When she got there
she met with this clown.

438
00:26:29,822 --> 00:26:31,182
MR. PENN: The
zoning commissioner.

439
00:26:31,256 --> 00:26:35,557
She had to have had his approval
for the wall and gate she built.

440
00:26:37,229 --> 00:26:38,629
(LAUGHS)

441
00:26:39,565 --> 00:26:43,627
She's making alliances with
politicians, building a fortress,

442
00:26:44,103 --> 00:26:47,369
all the while she's
pretending to be my friend.

443
00:26:48,474 --> 00:26:50,033
She's been planning a war.

444
00:27:01,153 --> 00:27:04,248
Victor, we'll be having a
chat with Miss Falcone.

445
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:08,116
Just so we are clear,
is this a chat, chat,

446
00:27:08,494 --> 00:27:11,555
or shove in the
trunk kinda chat?

447
00:27:13,932 --> 00:27:14,991
Get the shovel.

448
00:27:23,142 --> 00:27:24,610
(INDISTINCT TALKING)

449
00:27:27,212 --> 00:27:28,544
Mmm-mmm!

450
00:27:29,548 --> 00:27:32,279
I think I should rent an apartment
with all this money we're making.

451
00:27:32,451 --> 00:27:34,113
Do you have any
openings in your building?

452
00:27:34,186 --> 00:27:36,226
You know what you should
be doing with your winnings

453
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:39,348
is finding yourself a
neurologist, which I am not.

454
00:27:39,458 --> 00:27:40,619
It has to be you.

455
00:27:41,527 --> 00:27:42,527
You know me, Lee.

456
00:27:42,628 --> 00:27:44,105
You know what this
coconut is truly capable of.

457
00:27:44,129 --> 00:27:45,461
Which is why my answer is no.

458
00:27:50,502 --> 00:27:52,937
I know about your clinic.

459
00:27:56,041 --> 00:27:58,306
I'm guessing that
Cherry let you keep that

460
00:27:58,377 --> 00:28:01,211
as long as you work these fights.
That's the deal that you have, right?

461
00:28:02,014 --> 00:28:03,014
So?

462
00:28:04,116 --> 00:28:06,813
So, I'm guessing that that
means something to you,

463
00:28:06,885 --> 00:28:08,877
which makes you vulnerable to...

464
00:28:09,821 --> 00:28:10,821
To, um...

465
00:28:12,558 --> 00:28:13,719
To, um...

466
00:28:14,293 --> 00:28:17,058
- Blackmail and threats?
- Yes. Both of those.

467
00:28:17,162 --> 00:28:18,282
All right. So let's hear it.

468
00:28:18,430 --> 00:28:20,228
- What's your brilliant scheme?
- What?

469
00:28:20,332 --> 00:28:22,324
You said you wanted
to force me to help you.

470
00:28:22,401 --> 00:28:24,199
So, what is your threat?

471
00:28:24,570 --> 00:28:25,663
Hit me.

472
00:28:27,372 --> 00:28:30,604
If you don't help
me, I am going to...

473
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:37,240
Do something to that clinic.

474
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:39,010
(LAUGHS)

475
00:28:39,384 --> 00:28:41,910
- Oh, my God. You really aren't smart.
- God!

476
00:28:54,700 --> 00:28:56,396
(TRAIN HORN BLOWING)

477
00:29:16,054 --> 00:29:17,613
(RATS SQUEAKING)

478
00:29:37,175 --> 00:29:38,302
Jim.

479
00:29:59,998 --> 00:30:01,125
(GRUNTS)

480
00:30:02,301 --> 00:30:03,394
(WHIMPERING)

481
00:30:03,468 --> 00:30:06,927
Nakajima, hang tight, buddy.
We're gonna get you out of here.

482
00:30:13,812 --> 00:30:15,337
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

483
00:30:18,150 --> 00:30:19,150
Grenade!

484
00:30:19,418 --> 00:30:20,647
Run!

485
00:30:41,740 --> 00:30:42,740
Harvey?

486
00:30:47,346 --> 00:30:48,405
Harvey!

487
00:30:51,516 --> 00:30:53,348
Detective James Gordon.

488
00:30:54,052 --> 00:30:55,850
I hope you don't mind if I say,

489
00:30:56,154 --> 00:30:58,055
I'm tickled pink to meet you.

490
00:30:58,156 --> 00:31:01,285
I would shake your
hand, if it were possible.

491
00:31:01,793 --> 00:31:05,059
I'm a big fan. Big, big fan.

492
00:31:05,831 --> 00:31:07,663
Right. My biggest fan is a pig.

493
00:31:08,166 --> 00:31:09,657
Tell me where Harvey Bullock is.

494
00:31:09,868 --> 00:31:10,995
Oh!

495
00:31:11,169 --> 00:31:12,637
That dirty pig.

496
00:31:12,704 --> 00:31:14,832
Why do you waste
your time with him?

497
00:31:14,906 --> 00:31:16,169
He's holding you back.

498
00:31:17,042 --> 00:31:18,476
Or can you not see that?

499
00:31:19,044 --> 00:31:20,307
Oh!

500
00:31:20,379 --> 00:31:21,870
Never you fret.

501
00:31:22,848 --> 00:31:26,046
He's still alive, for
the time being anyway.

502
00:31:26,284 --> 00:31:32,019
But you, Detective, you
are safe as safe can be.

503
00:31:32,858 --> 00:31:33,882
You a cop?

504
00:31:33,959 --> 00:31:39,398
(LAUGHS) What? What
makes you think that?

505
00:31:40,699 --> 00:31:41,723
The things you knew,

506
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:44,292
the routes and schedules
of the cops you've killed.

507
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:48,062
If I were a policeman,

508
00:31:49,040 --> 00:31:52,477
you could, what, reason with me?

509
00:31:53,879 --> 00:31:56,007
Appeal to what we
have in common?

510
00:31:57,582 --> 00:31:59,915
Well, Jim... May I call you Jim?

511
00:32:00,385 --> 00:32:04,550
Jim, that's exactly
what I was going to do.

512
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:06,414
We have nothing in common.

513
00:32:06,792 --> 00:32:07,792
Oh.

514
00:32:08,093 --> 00:32:10,119
I beg to differ, <i>mon frère.</i>

515
00:32:10,595 --> 00:32:15,056
You and I both see all
too well the corruption,

516
00:32:15,233 --> 00:32:19,534
the filth inside the GCPD.

517
00:32:20,572 --> 00:32:24,703
You and I know that
Gotham cannot survive

518
00:32:25,444 --> 00:32:27,743
unless the cancer is cut out.

519
00:32:27,979 --> 00:32:30,915
We both share the same mission.

520
00:32:31,082 --> 00:32:34,109
Only I do it with a
little bit more flair.

521
00:32:34,653 --> 00:32:37,418
Killing Penguin's bagmen
won't change anything.

522
00:32:37,989 --> 00:32:39,355
It will for them.

523
00:32:39,624 --> 00:32:41,286
It will quite a bit.

524
00:32:42,461 --> 00:32:44,862
But, in the larger
scope, you're right.

525
00:32:45,130 --> 00:32:48,692
Which is why it
doesn't stop there.

526
00:32:49,100 --> 00:32:50,932
Not until I've butchered

527
00:32:51,002 --> 00:32:55,497
every single swine
on Penguin's payroll.

528
00:32:55,941 --> 00:32:57,842
That could be half
the department.

529
00:32:58,477 --> 00:33:00,070
I never said it would be pretty.

530
00:33:00,345 --> 00:33:02,678
Oh, it's the same old story.

531
00:33:03,014 --> 00:33:07,076
No one wants to see how the
sausage is made, but once it is made...

532
00:33:07,586 --> 00:33:08,610
Mmm.

533
00:33:08,687 --> 00:33:10,087
Isn't it delicious?

534
00:33:11,456 --> 00:33:12,456
Bite?

535
00:33:13,024 --> 00:33:15,459
You're delusional. You're
not doing this for Gotham,

536
00:33:15,527 --> 00:33:17,621
you're doing it for your
own demented reasons.

537
00:33:19,097 --> 00:33:23,626
My reasons are as
real as they come, Jim.

538
00:33:25,036 --> 00:33:28,097
I've suffered profound loss

539
00:33:28,874 --> 00:33:31,241
at the hands of the
greedy pigs in power.

540
00:33:32,711 --> 00:33:35,180
Profound!

541
00:33:37,082 --> 00:33:42,919
Then tell me, let me help
make it right, without all this.

542
00:33:43,021 --> 00:33:44,021
HARVEY: Jim!

543
00:33:44,489 --> 00:33:46,515
Oops. Got to go.

544
00:33:46,591 --> 00:33:47,671
HARVEY: Jim, where are you?

545
00:33:47,893 --> 00:33:49,521
Never you fear, Detective.

546
00:33:49,594 --> 00:33:52,086
You and I, we'll meet anon.

547
00:33:53,832 --> 00:33:55,164
Don't you touch him!

548
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:58,067
- Harvey!
- HARVEY: Jim!

549
00:33:58,503 --> 00:33:59,732
Backup's coming.

550
00:34:01,840 --> 00:34:02,899
Harvey.

551
00:34:22,060 --> 00:34:23,358
You heard Gordon, you freak.

552
00:34:23,428 --> 00:34:25,920
Backup's on the way.
You got one chance to run.

553
00:34:26,031 --> 00:34:27,932
Lies from a liar.

554
00:34:28,233 --> 00:34:29,929
They would have
been here by now.

555
00:34:30,735 --> 00:34:33,295
Besides, we both
know, Captain Bullock,

556
00:34:33,972 --> 00:34:35,406
you deserve this.

557
00:34:36,107 --> 00:34:37,268
(GORDON YELLS)

558
00:34:41,379 --> 00:34:42,574
Harvey.

559
00:34:45,717 --> 00:34:47,583
I do hate to cut and run.

560
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:49,086
(GROANS)

561
00:34:49,254 --> 00:34:50,313
Oopsie daisy!

562
00:34:50,622 --> 00:34:51,622
Hold on, partner.

563
00:34:54,759 --> 00:34:55,759
(CHOKING)

564
00:34:59,464 --> 00:35:01,228
Hold on, buddy. Hold on.

565
00:35:01,967 --> 00:35:04,732
- You're gonna be all right.
- Jim...

566
00:35:04,803 --> 00:35:07,102
You're gonna be all
right, I promise you.

567
00:35:07,439 --> 00:35:08,479
You're gonna be all right.

568
00:35:08,707 --> 00:35:10,107
(SIRENS WAILING)

569
00:35:10,909 --> 00:35:12,400
Hold on, buddy. Hold on.

570
00:35:13,278 --> 00:35:14,278
Hold on, pal.

571
00:35:18,550 --> 00:35:19,711
(WOMAN COUGHING)

572
00:35:20,418 --> 00:35:22,148
I can't miss any more
work. They'll fire me.

573
00:35:22,320 --> 00:35:25,813
It's okay. I'm gonna put you
on strong antibiotics, okay?

574
00:35:34,966 --> 00:35:36,025
Come on!

575
00:35:39,037 --> 00:35:40,630
(BABY CRYING)

576
00:35:53,385 --> 00:35:55,786
Oswald, I didn't know
you were coming over.

577
00:35:55,954 --> 00:35:57,115
I thought I'd surprise you.

578
00:35:59,557 --> 00:36:03,016
I'm sorry I had to cancel our
lunch yesterday. It was unavoidable.

579
00:36:03,395 --> 00:36:04,772
You have to let me
make it up to you.

580
00:36:04,796 --> 00:36:05,796
How about now?

581
00:36:06,831 --> 00:36:08,265
I was actually on my way out.

582
00:36:08,466 --> 00:36:09,466
Oh.

583
00:36:09,701 --> 00:36:10,862
Where to?

584
00:36:13,204 --> 00:36:16,697
This is going to sound
strange, but I can't tell you.

585
00:36:17,208 --> 00:36:19,302
Not yet. I want it
to be a surprise.

586
00:36:20,211 --> 00:36:21,211
The thing is...

587
00:36:24,816 --> 00:36:25,875
The cat's out of the bag.

588
00:36:27,052 --> 00:36:29,385
- I don't understand.
- I know what you're doing!

589
00:36:30,455 --> 00:36:31,855
The old Heritage Hotel,

590
00:36:32,157 --> 00:36:34,558
the fortress from which
you're going to attack me!

591
00:36:35,060 --> 00:36:36,688
What? No.

592
00:36:37,062 --> 00:36:39,657
Oh! Oh! Oh, so you weren't
pretending to be my friend

593
00:36:39,731 --> 00:36:41,563
while building your power base?

594
00:36:42,834 --> 00:36:44,928
(CHUCKLES) I should have known.

595
00:36:45,603 --> 00:36:50,598
But your father's blood
definitely runs through your veins.

596
00:36:51,176 --> 00:36:54,669
- Luckily, not for long.
- Oswald, you're making a mistake.

597
00:36:55,447 --> 00:36:56,847
I'm your friend.

598
00:36:58,216 --> 00:36:59,411
We'll see, won't we?

599
00:37:00,185 --> 00:37:02,416
Now, let's go see
what you're building.

600
00:37:02,854 --> 00:37:04,288
I can't wait!

601
00:37:08,860 --> 00:37:11,659
Barkeep, another grasshopper.

602
00:37:11,730 --> 00:37:12,730
Those won't help.

603
00:37:13,698 --> 00:37:15,724
- All right. Give me your money.
- What?

604
00:37:16,201 --> 00:37:18,670
The money you made... Well,
that he made. Give it to me.

605
00:37:24,542 --> 00:37:26,841
I don't make any promises,
but I'll see what I can do.

606
00:37:27,178 --> 00:37:31,548
Lee, I just gotta know. Why
did you change your mind?

607
00:37:32,217 --> 00:37:34,618
- Is it my charisma?
- Close.

608
00:37:35,687 --> 00:37:37,622
You asked what I was
doing in a place like this.

609
00:37:37,722 --> 00:37:40,590
I don't want to be here. I don't
want to be anywhere near Gotham.

610
00:37:40,792 --> 00:37:43,284
I left. But I
couldn't stay away.

611
00:37:44,462 --> 00:37:45,896
Because the Tetch virus,

612
00:37:45,964 --> 00:37:48,763
it hit The Narrows harder
than anywhere else.

613
00:37:48,833 --> 00:37:50,825
- So?
- So?

614
00:37:50,935 --> 00:37:52,164
It was my fault.

615
00:37:52,637 --> 00:37:54,731
Jim, tried to stop the
virus, and I didn't let him.

616
00:37:55,073 --> 00:37:56,974
I was infected, but nonetheless.

617
00:37:57,242 --> 00:38:00,644
I was there, I don't have a
choice. I have to be here.

618
00:38:00,745 --> 00:38:01,745
Wow.

619
00:38:04,282 --> 00:38:06,012
If you wanted to
blackmail me, by the way,

620
00:38:06,251 --> 00:38:09,415
what you should have done was taken
advantage of Grundy being popular.

621
00:38:09,788 --> 00:38:12,917
Threatened to take him away and
then Cherry, afraid of losing her star,

622
00:38:13,291 --> 00:38:14,816
would have forced
me to help you.

623
00:38:18,630 --> 00:38:21,293
Come by the clinic
tomorrow. We'll get started.

624
00:38:21,599 --> 00:38:22,897
Bye, pretty lady.

625
00:38:28,439 --> 00:38:30,135
Ed's gonna be smart again.

626
00:38:30,942 --> 00:38:33,173
Ed's gonna be smart?

627
00:38:34,145 --> 00:38:36,512
Ed's gonna be very smart.

628
00:38:37,115 --> 00:38:38,115
(CHUCKLES)

629
00:38:42,687 --> 00:38:43,687
It's okay, Charlie.

630
00:38:46,024 --> 00:38:47,024
Oswald...

631
00:38:49,494 --> 00:38:51,395
I want you to
know I forgive you.

632
00:38:51,830 --> 00:38:53,389
(CHILDREN CHATTERING)

633
00:38:57,402 --> 00:38:58,961
ZSASZ: Uh, boss?

634
00:39:00,738 --> 00:39:01,967
PENGUIN: What is this?

635
00:39:02,707 --> 00:39:03,707
What's happening?

636
00:39:03,875 --> 00:39:05,844
Huh. Kids...

637
00:39:10,982 --> 00:39:13,281
You started an orphanage?

638
00:39:14,686 --> 00:39:17,212
I wanted to surprise you next
week when everything was finished.

639
00:39:20,625 --> 00:39:22,651
WOMAN: Children,
back inside, please.

640
00:39:24,662 --> 00:39:28,190
Oswald, I want you to know I
understand the pressure you face.

641
00:39:29,133 --> 00:39:32,900
Your very survival depends on
seeing everyone as a potential threat.

642
00:39:33,571 --> 00:39:36,131
I watched my father
bear that weight for years.

643
00:39:38,376 --> 00:39:39,844
I don't want you
to end up like him.

644
00:39:42,580 --> 00:39:44,048
Sofia, please forgive me.

645
00:39:45,950 --> 00:39:47,009
How can I

646
00:39:47,785 --> 00:39:49,583
when I've already forgiven you?

647
00:39:52,223 --> 00:39:54,590
- Well, you do owe me one thing.
- Anything.

648
00:39:55,593 --> 00:39:56,593
Lunch.

649
00:39:57,428 --> 00:39:59,226
How do you feel
about mac and cheese?

650
00:40:01,132 --> 00:40:02,259
I love it.

651
00:40:06,037 --> 00:40:07,403
(MONITOR BEEPING)

652
00:40:11,976 --> 00:40:13,035
GORDON: Hi.

653
00:40:16,014 --> 00:40:17,014
Hey.

654
00:40:18,182 --> 00:40:19,741
You gave me quite
the scare back there.

655
00:40:19,851 --> 00:40:20,851
How you feeling?

656
00:40:24,355 --> 00:40:25,618
I've had better days.

657
00:40:28,559 --> 00:40:31,927
- Doc says you're gonna be okay.
- Shows what he knows.

658
00:40:33,298 --> 00:40:34,298
The Pyg?

659
00:40:36,034 --> 00:40:37,127
Son of a bitch.

660
00:40:38,403 --> 00:40:40,963
He could have killed me, but
he cut me just deep enough

661
00:40:41,072 --> 00:40:45,601
to make you choose, go after
him, or save my worthless hide.

662
00:40:46,611 --> 00:40:47,806
That wasn't a choice.

663
00:40:49,580 --> 00:40:51,071
Either way, I owe you.

664
00:40:54,585 --> 00:40:55,917
So pay it back now.

665
00:40:57,922 --> 00:40:59,185
Tell me the truth.

666
00:40:59,290 --> 00:41:01,282
How long have you been
taking money from Penguin?

667
00:41:03,695 --> 00:41:05,323
You knew Metzger was the bagman.

668
00:41:06,164 --> 00:41:07,689
You knew Nakajima was dirty.

669
00:41:09,200 --> 00:41:13,262
The Pyg says all this stuff
about you deserving to be killed.

670
00:41:15,940 --> 00:41:18,500
I don't know why I didn't see it
before, maybe I didn't want to.

671
00:41:22,680 --> 00:41:23,978
I just need to know how long?

672
00:41:25,650 --> 00:41:26,913
Are we talking years?

673
00:41:26,985 --> 00:41:30,353
No, just since this
license crap started.

674
00:41:32,256 --> 00:41:34,953
The commissioner
ordered us to comply.

675
00:41:36,461 --> 00:41:40,262
Then Metzger started showing up
with these envelopes stuffed full of cash.

676
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:44,162
I didn't do nothing I
wouldn't have done anyway.

677
00:41:46,971 --> 00:41:51,341
You gotta understand, Jim.
The bills I got, the debts I got.

678
00:41:52,643 --> 00:41:53,643
It stops.

679
00:41:56,014 --> 00:41:57,038
Stops now.

680
00:42:05,256 --> 00:42:08,658
REPORTER ON TV: <i>officers of
the GCPD have the city on high alert.</i>

681
00:42:08,860 --> 00:42:11,193
<i>Gotham finds itself
gripped by terror</i>

682
00:42:11,262 --> 00:42:13,424
<i>in the hands of a
ritualistic cop killer,</i>

683
00:42:13,531 --> 00:42:15,261
<i>being called Professor Pyg.</i>

684
00:42:15,733 --> 00:42:18,100
<i>He is still at large
after evading the police.</i>

685
00:42:18,403 --> 00:42:20,963
<i>The GCPD are urging
the people to remain calm</i>

686
00:42:21,039 --> 00:42:25,807
<i>and to report any suspicious
activity to GCPD Central Command.</i>

687
00:42:31,315 --> 00:42:35,377
THE PYG: "Two mother
pigs lived in a pen.

688
00:42:35,853 --> 00:42:38,049
"They each had four piglets

689
00:42:39,424 --> 00:42:40,892
"and that made ten.

690
00:42:41,859 --> 00:42:44,385
"All the piglets loved to play.

691
00:42:44,829 --> 00:42:49,494
"And they rolled and they
rolled in the mud all day.

692
00:42:50,935 --> 00:42:56,465
"At night with their
mothers curled up in a heap,

693
00:42:57,642 --> 00:43:00,612
"they squealed and they squealed

694
00:43:01,045 --> 00:43:04,038
"until they went...

695
00:43:05,650 --> 00:43:07,118
"to sleep.

696
00:43:08,619 --> 00:43:13,990
"And sleep well, for
tomorrow the ax shall fall."

697
00:43:54,599 --> 00:43:55,599
English - SDH
